# Human copy (no AI slop)

When writing or editing **user-facing** text (screens, paywall, Ember tips, website, Play Store paste, notifications), write like a clear person. Not a wellness coach or marketing LLM.

## Ban list

- Em dashes (`—`). Use a period, comma, colon, or middot (`·`).
- Soft filler: *gently, kindly, softly, quietly, whisper, soft presence, soft light, soft pride, breathe once, hold it soft, offered gently, presence made light*
- Coach clichés: *journey, deliberate(ly), glanceable, redefined, seamless, empower, unlock your, not a race, not a scorecard, not a demand, future self, ordinary moment, finite nature*
- Stacked hype lists and fake testimonials
- “And also”, “It’s important to note”, “In order to”, “Whether you’re…”

## Do this instead

- Short sentences. One idea per line when possible.
- Concrete product words: day %, widget, preview, subscribe, home screen.
- Prefer plain over poetic. Warm is fine; mystical is not.
- Empty UI placeholders may still use `—`.

```text
❌ The day is folding — you did enough. Soft pride, no pressure.
✅ Day’s almost done. Rest is fine.

❌ UNTIL makes time visible — so you spend it on purpose.
✅ UNTIL shows how much time you have left.
```

## Scope

Applies to visible strings only. Do **not** rewrite code comments or internal `docs/` architecture notes unless asked.
